<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>Biken Techno Corp, 20 million Swiss Francs unsecured with warrants due 2001, private placement, guaranteed by Sanwa Bank</p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Hokuetsu Paper Mills Ltd, 120 million Swiss Francs unsecured with warrants due 2001, private placement, guaranteed by Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank  </p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Hankyu Department Stores Inc, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2009</p>
<p>Toho Pharmaceutical Co Ltd, 60 million Swiss Francs unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Tokyo Sangyo Co Ltd, 0.2 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2000</p>
<p>Tsuchiya Home Co Ltd, 0.2 billion yen unsecured with warrants due 2001  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Showa Corp, 5 billion Euroyen unsecured convertible due 2004</p>
<p>Yachiyo Industry Co Ltd, five billion yen unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement</p>
<p>Yamada Denki Co Ltd, 70 million Swiss Francs unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement</p>
<p>-CC-</p>
<p>Nippon Soda Co Ltd, eight billion Euroyen unsecured convertible due 1999, private placement</p>
</text>
